---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import { SITE, LEGAL_UPDATED } from '../lib/site.js';

const sections = [
  { id: 'who-we-are', label: 'Who we are' },
  { id: 'what-we-collect', label: 'What we collect' },
  { id: 'why', label: 'Why we collect it' },
  { id: 'what-we-dont-do', label: 'What we never do' },
  { id: 'sharing', label: 'Who we share it with' },
  { id: 'retention', label: 'How long we keep it' },
  { id: 'security', label: 'How we protect it' },
  { id: 'your-rights', label: 'Your rights' },
  { id: 'cookies', label: 'Cookies and sessions' },
  { id: 'children', label: 'Children' },
  { id: 'changes', label: 'Changes to this policy' },
  { id: 'contact', label: 'Contact' },
];
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy policy"
  description="What CashIko collects, why, who it is shared with, how long it is kept, and the rights Philippine data privacy law gives you."
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Legal"
    title="Privacy policy"
    lead={`How CashIko handles your store's records. Last updated ${LEGAL_UPDATED}.`}
  />

  <div class="shell grid gap-12 py-12 md:grid-cols-[14rem_1fr] md:gap-16 md:py-16">
    <nav class="md:sticky md:top-28 md:self-start" aria-label="Policy sections">
      <p class="eyebrow">Contents</p>
      <ol class="mt-4 space-y-2">
        {sections.map((section, index) => (
          <li>
            <a href={`#${section.id}`} class="flex gap-2 text-[0.8125rem] text-forest-muted transition-colors hover:text-forest-dark">
              <span class="tabular text-[10px] text-warm">{String(index + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span>
              {section.label}
            </a>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ol>
    </nav>

    <article class="prose-legal max-w-2xl">
      <section id="who-we-are">
        <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
        <p>
          CashIko (“we”, “us”) provides a record-keeping service for small businesses in the Philippines. We are
          the personal information controller for the account and business data described here. You can reach us
          at <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
        </p>
        <p>
          This policy applies to the CashIko web application and this website. It is written with the Philippine
          Data Privacy Act of 2012 (Republic Act No. 10173), its implementing rules and regulations, and the
          issuances of the National Privacy Commission (NPC) in mind.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="what-we-collect">
        <h2>2. What we collect</h2>
        <h3>Account details</h3>
        <p>Your name, email address, and a hashed password. We never store passwords in readable form.</p>
        <h3>Business profile</h3>
        <p>
          Your store name, type of business, city or municipality, chosen language, plan, and the branches you
          create.
        </p>
        <h3>Records you create</h3>
        <p>
          Products and their costs and prices, sales and their line items, utang entries, payments, expenses,
          stock movements, and any notes you type. These are the records that make the service work.
        </p>
        <h3>Photos</h3>
        <p>
          If you upload a product photo, we store the file and serve it through a private, expiring link rather
          than a public address.
        </p>
        <h3>Technical data</h3>
        <p>
          IP address, browser type, session identifiers and basic server logs, used to keep you signed in,
          secure the service and diagnose faults.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="why">
        <h2>3. Why we collect it</h2>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>To provide the service</strong> — recording sales, computing stock and profit, tracking utang.</li>
          <li><strong>To operate your account</strong> — authentication, plan management, support replies.</li>
          <li><strong>To keep it secure</strong> — detecting abuse, preventing unauthorised access, maintaining backups.</li>
          <li><strong>To meet legal obligations</strong> — responding to lawful requests and accounting requirements.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          We rely on the performance of our contract with you, your consent where we ask for it, our legitimate
          interests in operating a secure service, and compliance with law.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="what-we-dont-do">
        <h2>4. What we never do</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>We do not sell your data, and we do not rent it.</li>
          <li>We do not pool one store’s numbers to advise or benchmark another store.</li>
          <li>We do not use your sales records for advertising.</li>
          <li>This website does not run advertising trackers or third-party analytics scripts.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section id="sharing">
        <h2>5. Who we share it with</h2>
        <p>
          We share data only with service providers who help us run CashIko, and only as far as needed:
          hosting and database providers, email delivery for account messages, and — on the Premium plan — the AI
          provider that generates assistant replies. When you ask the assistant a question, the question and the
          relevant business figures are processed to produce the answer.
        </p>
        <p>
          We may also disclose information where required by law, court order, or a lawful request from a
          competent authority, and where necessary to protect our rights or the safety of users.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="retention">
        <h2>6. How long we keep it</h2>
        <p>
          Business records are kept while your account is active, so that reports and history remain usable. If
          you close your account, we delete or anonymise personal data within a reasonable period, except where
          we must keep specific records to comply with the law or resolve a dispute. You can export your sales
          and reports to CSV before closing an account.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="security">
        <h2>7. How we protect it</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Passwords are stored as one-way hashes, never as plain text.</li>
          <li>Every record is scoped to the business account that created it.</li>
          <li>Product photos are private and served through expiring signed links.</li>
          <li>Access to production systems is limited to the team that operates the service.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          No system is perfectly secure. If a breach affects your personal data, we will notify you and the NPC
          as required by law.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="your-rights">
        <h2>8. Your rights</h2>
        <p>Under the Data Privacy Act you have the right to:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Be informed</strong> about how your data is processed.</li>
          <li><strong>Access</strong> the personal data we hold about you.</li>
          <li><strong>Correct</strong> inaccurate or incomplete data.</li>
          <li><strong>Object</strong> to processing, and to withdraw consent where processing is based on it.</li>
          <li><strong>Erasure or blocking</strong> of data no longer necessary for the purpose it was collected.</li>
          <li><strong>Data portability</strong> — obtain a copy in a structured, commonly used format.</li>
          <li><strong>Complain</strong> to the National Privacy Commission.</li>
          <li><strong>Damages</strong> where the law provides for them.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          To exercise any of these, email <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>. We may ask you to
          verify your identity before acting on a request.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="cookies">
        <h2>9. Cookies and sessions</h2>
        <p>
          CashIko uses a session cookie to keep you signed in and a CSRF token cookie to protect forms. These are
          required for the service to work. This marketing website does not set advertising cookies.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="children">
        <h2>10. Children</h2>
        <p>
          CashIko is intended for business owners and their staff. It is not directed at children, and we do not
          knowingly collect personal data from minors.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="changes">
        <h2>11. Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>
          If this policy changes in a way that affects your rights, we will post the updated version here and
          change the date at the top. Material changes will also be communicated in the app or by email.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section id="contact">
        <h2>12. Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about privacy, or a request under the Data Privacy Act:
          <a href={`mailto:${SITE.email}`}>{SITE.email}</a>.
        </p>
        <p>
          You may also contact the National Privacy Commission at
          <a href="https://www.privacy.gov.ph" rel="noopener">privacy.gov.ph</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
